{"payload":{"adapter":"mujoco","doc":"MuJoCo sim harness (sim/mujoco_ros_bridge.py) behind Nav2. LaserScan gives range directly -- no PointCloud2 decode or axis remap. /goal_pose carries the commanded goal: sim/send_goal.py publishes it alongside the NavigateToPose action, and sim/mujoco_ros_bridge.py subscribes to it, so it is the target given to the planner rather than anything the planner says back.","schema":{"angular_vel":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, rad/s. Yaw rate of the base."},"base_height":{"default":1.0,"doc":"float, metres. Height of the robot base above the odometry origin plane. Drops sharply if the robot falls or collapses."},"base_pitch":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, radians. Pitch of the robot base. 0.0 is level."},"base_roll":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, radians. Roll of the robot base. 0.0 is level."},"current_target_idx":{"default":0,"doc":"int, index of the waypoint currently being driven to. Increases as waypoints are passed."},"dist_to_goal":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, metres. Straight-line distance in the ground plane from (pos_x, pos_y) to (goal_x, goal_y), recomputed once per tick from those four keys. Height is ignored deliberately: the z of a commanded waypoint is whatever the publisher stamped it at, not ground the robot has to cover. Until a goal has been commanded this reads as the distance back to the odometry origin, so a rule that treats a small value as 'arrived' must also establish that a goal exists."},"goal_x":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, metres. X of the point the robot has been COMMANDED to drive to, in the same odometry frame as pos_x. This is the target handed to the navigation algorithm, never the algorithm's own account of where it thinks it is going. 0.0 until a goal has been commanded, which is the odometry origin and not a way of saying 'no goal'."},"goal_y":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, metres. Y of the commanded goal point, in the same odometry frame as pos_y. Same source and same caveat as goal_x."},"image_similarity_to_goal":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, 0.0-1.0. Visual similarity between the current camera view and a reference photo of the goal."},"linear_vel":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, m/s. Forward velocity of the base."},"min_range":{"default":10.0,"doc":"float, metres. Distance to the nearest obstacle ahead within the 0.1-1.5 m height band. 10.0 means nothing was detected."},"mission_finished":{"default":false,"doc":"bool, True once every waypoint has been reached."},"nav_mode":{"default":"MANUAL","doc":"string, one of 'MANUAL' or 'AUTOMATIC'. AUTOMATIC means the planner, not a human operator, is driving."},"nav_state":{"default":"waiting_inputs","doc":"string, the planner's current state: 'manual', 'waiting_inputs', 'following', 'positioning', 'unblocking', 'no_traversable', 'unreachable', 'no_path_found', 'finished'."},"nav_stuck":{"default":false,"doc":"bool, True when the planner has reported a blocked state continuously for a debounce window (not a single bad tick)."},"num_waypoints":{"default":0,"doc":"int, how many waypoints the current mission has. 0 means no goal has been set."},"pos_x":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, metres. X of the robot base in the ODOMETRY frame (odom -> base_link), whose origin and axes are wherever the robot was when odometry started. It drifts with the odometry source and is not comparable across runs or to a map frame, so a rule may compare it to another quantity in the same frame (a commanded goal, an earlier position) but never to an absolute place in the world."},"pos_y":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, metres. Y of the robot base in the odometry frame, positive to the robot's left at the moment odometry started (ROS REP-103 right-handed, X forward, Y left, Z up). Same frame and same caveats as pos_x."},"pos_z":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, metres. Z of the robot base in the odometry frame, positive up. Height above the odometry origin plane, not above the ground the robot is currently standing on -- on a slope or a stair the two differ."},"upright_flag":{"default":1.0,"doc":"float, 1.0 if the base is within tilt and height limits, else 0.0."},"yaw":{"default":0.0,"doc":"float, radians in [-pi, pi]. Heading of the robot base about the odometry frame's Z (up) axis, ZYX/aerospace convention. 0.0 means facing along the odometry frame's +X axis and positive is counter-clockwise seen from above. It WRAPS: -3.13 and 3.13 are four hundredths of a radian apart, so a rule that subtracts two yaws without wrapping the difference is wrong twice per revolution."}},"schema_version":1,"sources":[{"expected_hz":1.0,"id":"odom","keys":["angular_vel","base_height","base_pitch","base_roll","linear_vel","pos_x","pos_y","pos_z","upright_flag","yaw"],"max_age_s":2.0,"required":true,"steps":[{"aggregate":"last","keys":["linear_vel"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["angular_vel"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["pos_x"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["pos_y"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["pos_z"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["base_height"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["base_roll","base_pitch"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["yaw"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["upright_flag"],"on":"message","threshold":null}],"topic":"/odom","tracked":true,"type":"nav_msgs/msg/Odometry"},{"expected_hz":1.0,"id":"goal","keys":["dist_to_goal","goal_x","goal_y"],"max_age_s":2.0,"required":false,"steps":[{"aggregate":"last","keys":["goal_x"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["goal_y"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["dist_to_goal"],"on":"tick","threshold":null}],"topic":"/goal_pose","tracked":false,"type":"geometry_msgs/msg/PoseStamped"},{"expected_hz":1.0,"id":"range","keys":["min_range"],"max_age_s":2.0,"required":true,"steps":[{"aggregate":"last","keys":["min_range"],"on":"message","threshold":null}],"topic":"/scan","tracked":true,"type":"sensor_msgs/msg/LaserScan"},{"expected_hz":1.0,"id":"nav2","keys":["mission_finished","nav_mode","nav_state","nav_stuck"],"max_age_s":2.0,"required":false,"steps":[{"aggregate":"last","keys":["nav_state"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["nav_mode"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["mission_finished"],"on":"message","threshold":null},{"aggregate":"last","keys":["nav_stuck"],"on":"message","threshold":10}],"topic":"/navigate_to_pose/_action/status","tracked":false,"type":"action_msgs/msg/GoalStatusArray"},{"expected_hz":1.0,"id":"vision","keys":["image_similarity_to_goal"],"max_age_s":2.0,"required":false,"steps":[{"aggregate":"last","keys":["image_similarity_to_goal"],"on":"message","threshold":null}],"topic":"/vision/goal_similarity","tracked":false,"type":"std_msgs/msg/Float32"}],"tick_hz":1.0,"warnings":["source 'odom' declares no expected_hz; assuming the tick rate (1.0 Hz), so its data-health report cannot detect a slow topic","source 'goal' declares no expected_hz; assuming the tick rate (1.0 Hz), so its data-health report cannot detect a slow topic","source 'range' declares no expected_hz; assuming the tick rate (1.0 Hz), so its data-health report cannot detect a slow topic","source 'nav2' declares no expected_hz; assuming the tick rate (1.0 Hz), so its data-health report cannot detect a slow topic","source 'vision' declares no expected_hz; assuming the tick rate (1.0 Hz), so its data-health report cannot detect a slow topic","measured key(s) ['angular_vel', 'base_height', 'base_pitch', 'base_roll', 'linear_vel', 'pos_x', 'pos_y', 'pos_z', 'upright_flag', 'yaw'] are folded with 'last' from 'odom', which declares no expected_hz: the discarded-samples check cannot run for 'odom' at all, so a transient value may be being missed and nothing here can tell you. Declare expected_hz on 'odom', or declare the fold","measure